y 70 at half scale is already enough.\nL107:   * Trimming page weight before publishing, by re-encoding a hero JPEG as WEBP and reading the two file sizes directly against each other.\nL108:   * Preparing an email attachment where dropping to 50 percent scale saves far more than any quality setting would on its own.\nL109: ## ❓ Frequently Asked Questions\nL110: \nL111: Q Does my image get uploaded to a server?\nL112: \nL113: No. Compression happens entirely in your browser using the Canvas API. Your image never leaves your device.\nL114: \nL115: Q Which format compresses best?\nL116: \nL117: For photos, JPG or WEBP at 75–85 quality usually gives the smallest file with little visible loss. For graphics with transparency, use PNG or WEBP.\nL118: \nL119: Q Why is my PNG output not much smaller?\nL120: PNG is lossless, so compression is limited to re-encoding — it won't shrink as dramatically as JPG or WEBP. Scaling down the dimensions helps more for PNG.\nL121: \nL122: Q Will resizing affect quality?\nL123: \nL124: Reducing the scale reduces pixel dimensions, which lowers file size but also reduces the image's resolution. Use 100% if you need the original dimensions.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCompress Image to KB — JPG Compressor for Gov Forms | Free Digital Tools (https://freedigitaltools.in/tools/compress-image)\nciteturn5view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://freedigitaltools.in/tools/compress-image\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 47\nL0: 【0†Free Digital Tools】\nL1: \nL2: 【0†Home】【1†Exams】【2†Banking】【3†PDF Tools】【4†Image Tools】【5†Calculators】【6†Blog】【7†Identity】\nL3: \nL4: [Button: English][Button: हिन्दी]\nL5: \nL6: 【0†Home】›【4†Image Tools】\nL7: # Compress Image to KB\nL8: \nL9: Shrink any JPG, PNG, WEBP or HEIC photo to a specific KB target — 20 KB, 50 KB, 100 KB, anything you need for an upload form.\nL10: \nL11: [Input]\nL12: \nL13: 🗜️\nL14: \n